WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.095 --> 00:00:05.036
It’s club night at Valley Speedway.

2
00:00:05.036 --> 00:00:08.920
Heat 1 is done, and the driver says the car was loose off the corners.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:15.036
Here’s how to set up the Feature.

4
00:00:15.036 --> 00:00:22.520
Open the event, pick Feature in the session list, then press Add session.

5
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.039
Copy this session starts the Feature sheet from the Heat 1 setup.

6
00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:32.236
Results and feedback aren’t copied, so the Feature starts clean.

7
00:00:32.236 --> 00:00:38.781
First change: one click of rebound out of the RR shock.

8
00:00:38.781 --> 00:00:43.877
Then half a psi more in the RR tyre.

9
00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:49.301
And one degree more on the top wing.

10
00:00:49.301 --> 00:00:54.439
Long-press a number box for the quick add screen, with sixteenths and the team’s common values.

11
00:00:54.439 --> 00:01:06.470
Here, one and a quarter inches of block height.

12
00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.561
Each change shows what it was before.

13
00:01:08.561 --> 00:01:14.610
Tick Changes only to see just the changes.

14
00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:15.165
Press Save.

15
00:01:15.165 --> 00:01:22.694
It’s on the phone straight away, and syncs to the rest of the team when there’s signal.

